---
title: RCCService setup
description: How to set up RCCService, used for rendering images on the Site, and the Orbiter that runs it, for local development and production hosting.
---

This guide details how to set up RCCService for local development, moderation, and production publishing. More information, including general details on how RCC works, is available on the [RCCService service page](/services/rcc).

For the purposes of this guide, the [Orbiter](/services/rcc/#the-orbiter) will be used to start and manage the RCC process and all communications with it. This is the recommended setup for both development and production.

## Requirements

You will need:

- Latest version of [Git](https://git-scm.com) installed (expected as `git`, optional)
- Latest version of [Go](https://go.dev) installed (expected as `go`, [installation guide](/install/go))
- A terminal

## Instructions

{% steps %}

1. Clone the [tp-link-extender/RCCService](https://github.com/tp-link-extender/RCCService) repository to a directory of your choice on your local machine, and navigate to the root directory of the repository.

	```bash
	git clone https://github.com/tp-link-extender/RCCService
	cd RCCService
	```

   - If not using Git, you can also [download the repository as a compressed archive file](https://github.com/tp-link-extender/RCCService/archive/refs/heads/main.zip) (.zip) from the GitHub page and extract it to a directory of your choice.

2. Navigate to the **Orbiter** directory. Copy the **Orbiter/.env.example** file to **Orbiter/.env** and modify it to set up the environment variables.

3. Run `go build` to compile the Orbiter. This will produce an executable file in the same directory, either **Orbiter.exe** on Windows or **Orbiter** on Linux.

4. Copy both the compiled Orbiter executable and the **Orbiter/.env** file to their parent directory, the root of the repository. The Orbiter executable needs to be in the same directory as the **RCCService** folder to be able to start the RCC process correctly, and the **.env** file needs to be in the same directory as the Orbiter executable for it to read its configuration.

5. Run the Orbiter executable to start it and the RCC process. The Orbiter will automatically restart the RCC process if it crashes or is killed, and will print logs from both itself and the RCC process to the console.

{% /steps %}

If you're using RCC with Mercury Core, make sure that the [OrbiterPrivateURL](/guides/config#orbiterprivateurl) property points at the Orbiter's private port, including the appropriate scheme and port. The default value should work correctly if the Orbiter is running on the same machine as the Site. Set `ORBITER_KEY` to the same long, random value in both **Site/.env** and **Orbiter/.env**.
